================================================================================
Bundled image assets
================================================================================

Agent marks under public/images/agents/ are redistributed under their own
licenses. Each one's source, license, copyright owner and SHA-256 are recorded
in public/images/agents/asset-rights.json, with the corresponding license text
under licenses/.

  codex.svg        MIT  LobeHub contributors              licenses/lobehub-LICENSE
  opencode.svg     MIT  LobeHub contributors              licenses/lobehub-LICENSE
  claude-code.svg  MIT  LobeHub contributors              licenses/lobehub-LICENSE
  kilo-cli.svg     MIT  LobeHub contributors              licenses/lobehub-LICENSE
  openclaw.svg     MIT  Jason Young (cc-switch contributors)  licenses/cc-switch-LICENSE

An agent with no entry in asset-rights.json has no bundled mark and renders a
letter glyph instead. That is deliberate: a vendor favicon copied in without an
auditable redistribution basis would be both a licensing and a trademark
problem, so the absence of a mark is the correct state rather than a gap.

Screenshots under public/images/guide/ are screen captures of macOS system UI,
showing what the operating system displays when it blocks an unsigned
application. The interface elements pictured are the property of Apple Inc. They
are included to document the operating system's own behaviour, which the
first-launch guide cannot be followed without; no endorsement or affiliation is
implied. Each one's contents and SHA-256 are recorded in
public/images/guide/asset-rights.json. They contain no account name, device name
or other identifying detail.

